WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.145 --> 00:00:02.346
(accordion music)

00:00:02.346 --> 00:00:05.638
- Ah, I'm tell you, I feel
sorry if I have to retire.

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:07.049
You know why?

00:00:07.049 --> 00:00:09.451
I have so many customers that say,

00:00:09.451 --> 00:00:11.108
"Alex, you never retire."

00:00:11.108 --> 00:00:13.950
I say, "No, one day I'll
have to retire, no?"

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:16.783
(accordion music)

00:00:23.579 --> 00:00:26.586
(Greek style accordion music)

00:00:26.586 --> 00:00:28.458
My name is Alex Carozza

00:00:28.458 --> 00:00:31.867
and I fix accordions
since 1960 in New York.

00:00:31.867 --> 00:00:33.674
The people comes from all over the world

00:00:33.674 --> 00:00:35.953
to fix the accordion cause they say

00:00:35.953 --> 00:00:37.587
that I'm the best, I don't know.

00:00:37.587 --> 00:00:38.712
(chuckles)

00:00:38.712 --> 00:00:40.764
This sometime breaks, you have to change.

00:00:40.764 --> 00:00:42.301
Very difficult.

00:00:42.301 --> 00:00:43.856
I'm the only one in New York that

00:00:43.856 --> 00:00:46.106
fix accordions in this moment, you know?

00:00:46.106 --> 00:00:48.519
See, I fix the accordion
and I lose the customer

00:00:48.519 --> 00:00:50.690
because I fix the accordion correctly.

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:53.266
(laughs)

00:00:53.266 --> 00:00:54.222
Honest.

00:00:54.222 --> 00:00:55.818
I have this one for example, take a look.

00:00:55.818 --> 00:00:57.611
This is a very old accordion.

00:00:57.611 --> 00:00:58.444
Ooh.

00:00:58.444 --> 00:01:00.913
At least this accordion is 75 years old.

00:01:00.913 --> 00:01:02.396
- [Interviewer] How old are you?

00:01:02.396 --> 00:01:04.324
- Ha, if I tell you, you won't believe it.

00:01:04.324 --> 00:01:05.665
I'm 88.

00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:06.841
You believe it?

00:01:06.841 --> 00:01:08.202
I swear.

00:01:08.202 --> 00:01:09.452
How old is him?

00:01:10.644 --> 00:01:12.784
If I tell you 93 you won't believe it.

00:01:12.784 --> 00:01:14.663
We working together 60 years.

00:01:14.663 --> 00:01:16.018
Since 1949.

00:01:16.018 --> 00:01:17.558
(laughs)

00:01:17.558 --> 00:01:19.553
- Like yesterday, yeah?

00:01:19.553 --> 00:01:21.843
- Yeah, looks like yesterday right?

00:01:21.843 --> 00:01:24.676
(accordion music)

00:01:26.470 --> 00:01:29.646
You gotta understand,
an instrument is like a

00:01:29.646 --> 00:01:31.273
some part of your life.

00:01:31.273 --> 00:01:34.673
You care for the instrument
more than anything else.

00:01:34.673 --> 00:01:37.269
I love this more than anything else.

00:01:37.269 --> 00:01:39.986
It's not the money sometimes in life.

00:01:39.986 --> 00:01:43.615
If you are healthy and
happy, money doesn't count.

00:01:43.615 --> 00:01:44.622
This is what I believe.

00:01:44.622 --> 00:01:46.834
Maybe I'm wrong but,

00:01:46.834 --> 00:01:50.628
now you have all my secrets (chuckling).

00:01:50.628 --> 00:01:51.461
It's good.

00:01:51.461 --> 00:01:53.122
(accordion music)

00:01:53.122 --> 00:01:54.104
Just like that.

00:01:54.104 --> 00:01:56.187
(laughs)

00:01:58.338 --> 00:01:59.171
Okay.

